  3. durations: a number followed by s or ms (`1.23s`, `45ms`) -> <DUR>;
  4. UUIDs (invocation ids, command ids) -> <UUID>; the time of day in the client's log
     prefix `[LEVEL HH:MM:SS.mmm file:line]` -> `[LEVEL <TIME> file:line]`;
  5. sandbox directory numbers `/sandbox/<strategy>/N/` -> `/sandbox/<strategy>/<N>/`;
